language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ allergy: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Four friends (two women named Debra and Janet, and two men named Hugh and Rick) found that each of them is allergic to something different: eggs, mold, nuts and ragweed. We would like to match each one's surname (Baxter, Lemon, Malone and Fleet) with his or her allergy. We know that: Rick is not allergic to mold; Baxter is allergic to eggs; Hugh is neither surnamed Lemon nor Fleet; Debra is allergic to ragweed; Janet (who isn't Lemon) is neither allergic to eggs nor to mold.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/allergy.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the friend (Debra = 0, Janet = 1, Hugh = 2, Rick = 3) allergic to eggs, mold, nuts and ragweed
find eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed : int(0..3)
$ the friend (Debra = 0, Janet = 1, Hugh = 2, Rick = 3) with surname Baxter, Lemon, Malone and Fleet
find baxter, lemon, malone, fleet : int(0..3)

branching on [eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed, baxter, lemon, malone, fleet]

such that
$ each friend has exactly one allergy, so the four allergies belong to four different friends
allDiff([eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed]),
$ each friend has exactly one surname, so the four surnames belong to four different friends
allDiff([baxter, lemon, malone, fleet]),
$ Rick (3) is not allergic to mold
mold != 3,
$ Baxter is allergic to eggs: the friend surnamed Baxter is the friend allergic to eggs
baxter = eggs,
$ Hugh (2) is neither surnamed Lemon nor Fleet
lemon != 2,
fleet != 2,
$ Debra (0) is allergic to ragweed
ragweed = 0,
$ Janet (1) is not surnamed Lemon
lemon != 1,
$ Janet (1) is neither allergic to eggs nor to mold
eggs != 1,
mold != 1
